<p>Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said the United States has no “definitive time frame” for ending the war against Iran and that President Trump will decide when US objectives have been met. At the same time, multiple outlets said the Pentagon is seeking more than $200 billion in additional funding from Congress for the war, although Hegseth said the figure could still change and the White House had not yet formally sent the request to lawmakers. The funding push suggests a military campaign that could last longer and cost more than officials first presented, and it is already facing resistance on Capitol Hill as Congress weighs both the price tag and the open-ended timeline. Trump later confirmed he would ask Congress for the $200 billion, calling it “a small price to pay,” while administration officials said the money would help sustain operations and replenish weapons stocks used in the conflict.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/HXU1VfcTzzE185pwF_1bY9g6PdcpszziKiwAs_9JWyeAKRKQRBczzVE0JC4tNJy-h8UOxnbqn4TWryobPqVfj1wUQ17rq4lR6f6gIt0YyYeRbwhWrI6fPiR2zn88EYR4XErkjL4318rMyxYYH5nba2to-fkCWP2v-kmOGLL-U2MXyLrhfpQHkcgFlZHvo9bS3ZflkFUXWUI' alt='Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth speaking to reporters on Thursday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Senate hurdle: Any large supplemental package is likely to face a tough path in the Senate, where supporters would probably need 60 votes and where lawmakers in both parties have signaled reluctance or opposition.</li><li>Early costs: The United States spent more than $11 billion in the war’s first week alone, according to reporting cited by multiple outlets, underscoring how fast the costs have mounted.</li><li>Scale: RT, citing Washington Post reporting, said the proposed package, combined with money already spent, could push the war’s total cost above half of Iran’s 2025 GDP, which it put at $356.5 billion.</li></ul><blockquote>We wouldn’t want to set a definitive time frame. - Pete Hegseth</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pentagon: Asked about the reported request, Pete Hegseth defended the need for more wartime spending, saying, “it takes money to kill bad guys.” (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/it-takes-money-to-kill-bad-guys-hegseth-says-as-pentagon-seeks-billions-in-additional-funds-for-the-iran-war'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Trump said there were “a lot of reasons” to seek extra war funding, but he did not publicly spell them out when asked about the request. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/mar/19/donald-trump-iran-bondi-epstein-mullin-japan-takaichi-save-voter-id-latest-news-updates'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Democratic critics: Sen. Chris Van Hollen publicly opposed the proposal, calling $200 billion for the war “an absolute nonstarter” and arguing that Americans do not want the conflict. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/635529-pentagon-iran-extra-funding/'>RT</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/19/hegseth-says-no-timeframe-for-war-on-iran-as-pentagon-asks-for-200bn'>Hegseth says no ‘timeframe’ for war on Iran as Pentagon asks for $200bn</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/it-takes-money-to-kill-bad-guys-hegseth-says-as-pentagon-seeks-billions-in-additional-funds-for-the-iran-war'>WATCH: &#x27;It takes money to kill bad guys,&#x27; Hegseth says as Pentagon seeks billions more for the Iran war</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/635529-pentagon-iran-extra-funding/'>Pentagon wants $200 billion Iran war chest – WaPo</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-hegseth-says-it-takes-money-to-kill-bad-guys-when-asked-about-pentagon/'>Hegseth says &#x27;it takes money to kill bad guys&#x27; when asked about Pentagon Iran war funding request</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3347215/us-has-no-end-date-iran-war-strikes-very-much-track-hegseth'>US has no end date for Iran war, strikes ‘very much on track’: Hegseth</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/03/19/qzqr-m19.html'>Trump’s $200 billion Iran funding request points to massive scale of war plans</a> - wsws.org</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-israel-usa-war-live-updates-march-19-2026/article70760463.ece'>Iran-Israel war LIVE: Netanyahu to hold press conference; second since beginning of the war</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/19/world/middleeast/pentagon-200-billion-iran-war-funding-hegseth.html'>Pentagon Seeks Additional $200 Billion to Fund Iran War</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/no-definitive-timeframe-to-end-iran-war-pentagon-chief-11239484#publisher=newsstand'>&#x27;No Definitive Timeframe To End Iran War&#x27;: Pentagon Chief</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/mar/19/donald-trump-iran-bondi-epstein-mullin-japan-takaichi-save-voter-id-latest-news-updates'>Trump confirms he will ask Congress for $200bn to fund war on Iran, calling it ‘a small price to pay’ – US politics live</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>